---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="R Workbench — CMNA"
  description="Run real R and selected CMNA algorithms directly in your browser with webR."
>
  <header class="page-head workbench-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">CMNA Laboratory</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">This is R. Go nuts.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Write valid R, run it locally in your browser, and use selected CMNA functions
        without sending your code to a computation server.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="workbench-primer">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Actual R, not R-shaped JavaScript</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">The browser is the R machine.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Local execution</strong>
          <p>
            webR runs R through WebAssembly in your browser. Your code is evaluated
            on your device; CMNA does not send it to a remote R server.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="r-workbench" data-r-workbench>
        <div class="r-toolbar">
          <div class="r-runtime">
            <span class="r-runtime-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span data-r-status>Preparing R…</span>
          </div>

          <div class="r-toolbar-actions">
            <label>
              Example
              <select data-r-examples>
                <option value="">Choose one…</option>
                <option value="bisection">CMNA bisection</option>
                <option value="newton">CMNA Newton</option>
                <option value="matrix">Base R matrix / eigenvalues</option>
                <option value="plot">Arbitrary function + plot</option>
                <option value="wilkinson">Wilkinson's polynomial</option>
                <option value="himmelblau">Himmelblau function</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <button class="r-reset" type="button" data-r-reset>Reset R session</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="r-editor-shell">
          <div class="r-editor-label">
            <span>R</span>
            <small>⌘/Ctrl + Enter to run</small>
          </div>
          <textarea
            class="r-editor"
            data-r-editor
            spellcheck="false"
            autocomplete="off"
            aria-label="R code editor"
          >f <- function(x) {
  exp(-x^2) * cos(7 * x)
}

f(c(-1, 0, 1))

curve(
  f,
  from = -3,
  to = 3,
  n = 500,
  xlab = "x",
  ylab = "f(x)"
)</textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="r-run-row">
          <button class="button r-run" type="button" data-r-run disabled>Run R</button>
          <span class="r-timing" data-r-timing></span>
        </div>

        <div class="r-results">
          <section>
            <div class="r-result-heading">
              <h2>Console</h2>
              <span>stdout / stderr</span>
            </div>
            <div class="r-output" data-r-output aria-live="polite">
              <div class="r-output-line">R output will appear here.</div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section>
            <div class="r-result-heading">
              <h2>Plots</h2>
              <span>captured from R graphics</span>
            </div>
            <div class="r-plots" data-r-plots>
              <p>No plot yet.</p>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="workbench-notes">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>CMNA functions already loaded</h3>
          <p>
            This first workbench bundle includes <code>bisection</code>,
            <code>newton</code>, <code>secant</code>, <code>wilkinson</code>, and
            <code>himmelblau</code> from the companion package. More of the package
            can move into the browser as the laboratory expands.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Your session persists</h3>
          <p>
            Define a function or object, run it, and it remains in the R global
            environment for the next command. The Reset button reloads the page and
            starts a fresh R session.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>You can hurt your own tab</h3>
          <p>
            GitHub Pages cannot provide webR's cross-origin-isolated interrupt
            channel, so an infinite loop cannot be cleanly interrupted. Reloading
            the page terminates the session. This is a local browser problem, not a
            CMNA server problem.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="workbench-source-note">
        Runtime: <a href="https://docs.r-wasm.org/webr/latest/">webR</a>.
        Canonical CMNA package source:
        <a href="https://github.com/k3jph/cmna-pkg">github.com/k3jph/cmna-pkg</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline type="module" src="/js/r-workbench.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
